## 6. Conclusion

The five cases demonstrate the importance of evaluating seriousness and expectedness independently during pharmacovigilance assessment.

Among the five reported cases, three were classified as serious and two as non-serious. Expectedness was identified as expected for amoxicillin and ibuprofen, and unexpected for metformin, according to the poster. The expectedness classifications for atorvastatin and levofloxacin require verification.

This exercise highlights the importance of accurate ADR documentation, regulatory seriousness criteria and reference product information in patient safety monitoring.

